[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42559"] :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-2){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-28+40) \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120474 :question/answer-fields 17592186119318] {:db/id "q-91220/selection/ma-v1/99384de3f1f1d9e92c86409322bc733a9f32db0abdd1ee353fd71e9158cffaa4/298a0faf60e26b9e69061203d85fcc2bb83b218312361e851a4d1b57b64dc4d8" :answer/id #uuid "bf520dcf-d62d-5fee-8732-8209